WEBVTT

00:00:27.607 --> 00:00:33.071
his face obscured by a beak-like mask,
his body covered from head to toe.

00:00:33.571 --> 00:00:36.657
He examines you 
and even without seeing his face,

00:00:36.657 --> 00:00:38.493
you know the diagnosis:

00:00:38.493 --> 00:00:39.786
you have the plague.

00:00:39.786 --> 00:00:44.373
The plague stands out as one of the most 
terrifying and destructive diseases

00:00:44.373 --> 00:00:45.833
in human history.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.838
It swept across large parts of Afro-
Eurasia in three separate pandemics

00:00:50.838 --> 00:00:54.967
starting in the 6th, 14th,
and 19th centuries;

00:00:55.176 --> 00:00:57.929
killed tens of millions of people,

00:00:57.929 --> 00:01:02.683
and had— in the best of cases— 
about a 40% survival rate.